{
  "id": "COMPOUND:27606 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Pseudoaeruginosin KT554 is implicated in the regulation of Phosphodiesterase 6C through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that the compound acts as a target for multiple entities, with CAKI-2 serving as a common intermediate in these relationships. CAKI-2 is known to be a target of 3-Methylhexan-1-ol and (1S,9S,10R,12R,13S,14S)-5,5,9,13-tetramethylpentacyclo[11.2.1.01,10.04,9.012,14]hexadecan-6-one, both of which directly target Phosphodiesterase 6C. This indicates that Pseudoaeruginosin KT554 may exert its effects through a shared mechanism involving the activation or inhibition of Phosphodiesterase 6C, potentially through the modulation of downstream signaling pathways. The consistent presence of CAKI-2 as a target across different pathways suggests a possible role in the compound's pharmacological action, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
